A||||12||88formula||Dogbone does not line up, need your help||||1||
Z||000000||88formula||07-08-2001||07:23 PM||||This is a 3.4-liter engine in my car. When I put the engine in today I noticed that the brackets for the dogbone do not line up properly. Everything else seems to fit fine except this. Anyone ever experience this after an engine swap?<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dogbone.JPG"> <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Songman||07-08-2001||07:41 PM||||In the picture it doesn't look all that bad. But if it looks worse in person and you think it might be a problem, I would suggest that you need to do some adjusting on your motor and tranny mounts. They may be sitting a little bit out of line. There was a thread going on about how they are supposed to be adjusted last week.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||07-08-2001||10:44 PM||||I'll check that out. It's out about 1/4 inch. I'm just tired of being under that car. I've been working on this thing for five days straight installing a rebuilt 3.4-liter engine.||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||07-08-2001||11:54 PM||||It looks to me that your biggest problem here is that the nut looks like it would rub up against the strut tower with engine vibration.<P>What about loosening the brackets?  Those holes <I>might</I> have a little bit of adjustment in them, or you could always elongate the holes to <B>make</B> them have adjustment!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroMaster88||07-09-2001||01:01 AM||||Mine was a little off (bout quarter inch) after we put the 2.8 in my car.  I just put it in place and bolted it down.  It is fine so far.<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">         <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe 30,000 miles||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||07-09-2001||07:30 AM||||Looks to me from pic, that you just need to adjust the other mounts. The engine appears to be a little cocked.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Elvira||07-09-2001||11:12 AM||||Chester's was the same way when we put the new motor in.  We replaced all mounts with poly ones so it was a b**ch to line up the dogbone.  After alot of pushing, cussing, and slamming knuckles, it finally went in.  No problems at all out of it.<P>------------------<BR>Elvira<BR>Blue 87GT<BR>Black 86GT 5sp x 2<BR>86SC t-top 58k miles||||reg||1
Z||000007||Leadfoot||07-09-2001||01:56 PM||||Did you install new mounts?  My dogbone looked the same until I found out that I had a bad tranny mount.  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Will||07-09-2001||03:50 PM||||Do you have the engine mount studs in the right set of holes in the cradle? There are two sets of holes available for the forward transmission mount, and I think also two sets for the engine mount.||||reg||1
Z||000009||88formula||07-09-2001||04:20 PM||||The engine looks cocked because the trunk liner is bent giving the false illusion that the engine is cocked. The misarranged dogbone is caused by one of two things. The rear transmission mount is in the wrong hole or the mounts just need to be adjusted. The engine mounts are the original mounts. They are in very good condition since they only have 50k on them.<P>Thanks for the help guys. BTW which set of holes does the rear transmission mount belong in?<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Alex4mula||07-09-2001||04:42 PM||||When I did my 3.4 everything aligned ok. I installed 2/3 new mounts at that time. Also I used the stock (2.8) front engine mount bracket. Which one you used? The tranny mounts has some play as some mentioned already. Just a little adjustment should do.<P>------------------<BR>Alex4mula<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/p69fbfe3e99ec5a0b81c10afcc578ff95/fe6d5c42.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||88formula||07-09-2001||05:02 PM||||I used the original 88 front engine bracket. I modified it a little to clear the 3.4 oil pan. I had a bolt welded to an earlier year engine shock mount and modified that so that the front engine mount would bolt over it. I didn't like the idea of using an earlier front mount, which only has two mounting points, with what I have now I retained the original four mounting points and it’s as strong as the original. It is the original! ||||reg||1
Z||000012||88formula||07-09-2001||08:59 PM||||I got it. I loosened the bolts on all the motor mounts and pried the engine over until the dogbone lined up perfectly. It sits just right now. <P>Thanks for the advice.<BR>||||reg||1
